From 01907bfa6f5ebf8434e0097644cb5fe1bc453c8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 08:02:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] chronik: native extension subscription groups and WS script
 types

Tier extensions can now add their own subscription groups and the WsSub
script types those groups serve, through the SubscriptionHub passed to
Extension::RegisterWsScriptTypes once at indexer startup.

- Subs notifies extension groups after the script group and before the
  token ID group, and counts them in the block-event short-circuit.
- A WsSub script subscription whose type name and payload size match a
  registered type subscribes to that group with the payload as member;
  other payload sizes fall through to the core script types. Several
  type names may share one group.
- WS sessions drain extension receivers after scripts and before token
  and LOKAD IDs, count them against the subscription limits and release
  them on unsubscribe and close.

The eCash tier registers no extension, so its behavior is unchanged.

Tier: eCash

Coordinator integration provenance (metrics369):
Retain both extension subscription test additions and earlier observer lifecycle control when replaying the later test-file tail.
All build/runtime/observer controls deferred by user compile-first policy; ordered source replay is not runtime approval.
